Relax the pydicom<3 cap to allow pydicom 3.x.

dicom-anonymizer 1.0.13 uses only modern pydicom APIs (dcmread, generate_uid,
multival.MultiValue) — none of the deprecated read_file/write_file aliases that
pydicom 3 removed. Verified functionally against pydicom 3.0.2: anonymize_dataset
cleanly anonymizes CT/MR/RTPLAN/EMRI/liver test datasets (PatientName cleared,
SOPInstanceUID regenerated) with no errors. The <3 cap was conservative, not a
real incompatibility, and it blocks installation on Fedora (which ships
pydicom 3.x).

Upstream: https://github.com/KitwareMedical/dicom-anonymizer
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -43,6 +43,6 @@
     #
     # For an analysis of "install_requires" vs pip's requirements files see:
     # https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/distributing-packages-using-setuptools/
-    install_requires=["pydicom<3", "tqdm"],  # Optional
+    install_requires=["pydicom>=2", "tqdm"],  # Optional
     extras_require={"dev": ["pytest", "bs4", "fire", "requests", "pre-commit", "ruff"]},
 )
